{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q409903","formula":"Cl₃Nd","hill":"Cl3Nd","elements":["Cl","Nd"],"composition":{"Cl":3.0,"Nd":1.0},"names":{"en":"Neodymium chloride","ru":"Хлорид неодима(III)"},"descriptions":{"en":"Neodymium(III) chloride or neodymium trichloride is a chemical compound of neodymium and chlorine with the formula NdCl3. This anhydrous compound is a mauve-colored solid that rapidly absorbs water on exposure to air to form a purple-colored hexahydrate, NdCl3·6H2O. Neodymium(III) chloride is produced from minerals monazite and bastnäsite using a complex multistage extraction process. The chloride has several important applications as an intermediate chemical for production of neodymium metal and neodymium-based lasers and optical fibers.","ru":"Хлорид неодима(III) — бинарное неорганическое соединение, соль металла неодима и соляной кислоты с формулой NdCl3, розово-фиолетовые кристаллы, растворимые в воде, образует кристаллогидраты."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":66204,"mass":250.6,"charge":0,"smiles":"Cl[Nd](Cl)Cl","inchikey":"ATINCSYRHURBSP-UHFFFAOYSA-K","iupac":"trichloroneodymium","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-23183","atoms":8,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[7.475,0.0,0.0],[-3.737,6.473,0.0],[0.0,0.0,4.249]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":3.737,"y":2.158,"z":3.187,"el":"Nd"},{"x":0.0,"y":4.316,"z":1.062,"el":"Nd"},{"x":1.96,"y":4.51,"z":3.187,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.549,"y":3.952,"z":1.062,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.778,"y":1.964,"z":1.062,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.812,"y":2.522,"z":3.187,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-1.148,"y":5.916,"z":3.187,"el":"Cl"},{"x":4.885,"y":0.558,"z":1.062,"el":"Cl"}],"bonds":[[0,3,1],[0,7,1],[1,2,1],[1,6,1],[0,4,1],[1,5,1],[1,4,1],[0,2,1]],"cellOrigin":[0,0,0]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q409903","